The difference between intrinsic and extrinsic magic already exists
as atheist conduct.  If it's the player character casting the spell
then
it is atheistic.  If the player gets the diety to do the magic
(artifact
creation and whatnot) then it's religion.

As such muggle combat could be anywhere in the range from never
*succeeding* in a spell cast based on the behavior of squibs in the
Potter-verse through never attempting to cast a spell and so on.  One
step would be wands.  They count as magic use in the Potter-verse
though their mechanics are different than in Nethack.

So it could range from never cast a spell through never used up a
magical charge on an item.  I do not think using an unlimited resource
like a magic whistle or unihorn would count but exactly how strict
is a matter of tastes.


